  "details": "It would be amazing if we could get an outward-facing url to our in-game calendar in ics form. This would allow users to subscribe to their calendar in whatever service they are already using. Like Thunderbird, Google calendar, iCloud calendar, etc etc.\n\nThis would make it easier to cross-check when events starts in vrchat and what other obligations in life you have without having to compare two calendars. (Especially since one of them starts on a Sunday *cough*)\n\nSo if we would do this. It would be pretty neat if we could access it like this or similar. Being able to get the url from your settings page on the website.\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/calendar/SGkhIEkgaG9wZSB5b3UgYXJlIGRvaW5nIGdvb2Qu\n\nAnd if that link would lead to an ics that updates when we add or remove posts in our calendar. Or we have an event update the calendar details. We get automatic updates to wherever we have it added Which is pretty neat!",
